    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The inspector will document any new damages found during the re-inspection.</p>
  </div>
</div>

	<p>To ensure the vehicle's mileage matches the information provided in the LR bill of lading, the following process will be followed:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Odometer reading will be recorded on the handover document.</li>
		<li>The recipient will be asked to verify the recorded odometer reading against the vehicle's odometer.</li>
		<li>If the recorded reading matches the recipient's verification, the odometer verification is considered successful.</li>
		<li>If there is a discrepancy, further investigation may be required to determine the cause of the difference (e.g., incorrect reading or tampering).</li>
	</ul>

	<p>To ensure the delivered vehicle's condition matches the initial pickup photos, the following steps will be taken:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>The recipient will be provided with the pickup photos for reference.</li>
		<li>The recipient will examine the delivered vehicle in daylight conditions and compare it to the pickup photos.</li>
		<li>Any discrepancies between the delivered vehicle's condition and the pickup photos will be documented on the handover document.</li>
		<li>The recipient will sign off on the handover document, acknowledging the comparison with the pickup photos and any identified discrepancies.</li>
	</ul>

	<p>Upon successfully completing the daylight condition re-inspection, odometer verification, and comparison with pickup photos, the recipient will sign off on the handover document:</p></div>
